# strings5 — MSET / MGET and key naming
#
# Learn: keys are one flat namespace, so the convention is
# object-type:id:field, separated by colons (product:42:price). Tools and
# SCAN patterns (product:*:price) rely on that shape. MSET and MGET set or
# fetch many keys in one round trip instead of one command per key.
#
# Task: store the prices of products 1, 2 and 3 (9.99, 24.50, 3.75) under
# product:<id>:price with ONE MSET, then print all three with ONE MGET in
# the order 1, 2, 3. The current file uses ad-hoc key names and five
# separate commands.
#

SET price_product1 9.99
SET product2Price 24.50
SET product:3 3.75
GET price_product1
GET product2Price
